.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
Optional shapes, filtering, sensors and contacts for a \fBSprite\fP, \fBPart\fP or \fBParticle\fP\&. 


.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
\fBAPI Stability: 2 — Evolving\fP\&. This API is implemented and supported, but its contract is still settling\&. Compatibility is preserved where practical; breaking changes are documented in release notes\&. See \fBAPI stability\fP\&.
.RE
.PP
Use \fBSprite::setupCollider()\fP, \fBPart::setupCollider()\fP or \fBParticle::setupCollider()\fP\&. Their read-only \fRcollider\fP property returns the same handle until removeCollider(); beforehand it returns shared \fBCollider::NoCollider\fP\&. \fBCollider\fP is independent of animation, artwork and physical motion\&. Creating one never creates a \fBPhysicsBody\fP\&.

.PP
Local circles, capsules, rectangles and polygons follow their owner's affine transform, including parent/bone motion, scale and reflection\&. Nonuniformly scaled or sheared circles and capsules use convex approximations; see \fBcollider_capsule_geometry\fP\&. Singular geometry does not participate in the collision world\&. \fBgetBounds()\fP, \fBcontains()\fP and \fBoverlaps()\fP are explicit geometric queries and ignore event filters\&.

.PP
Enable \fBSpriteLayer::enableCollisions()\fP for contacts within a layer, or \fBSpriteLayer::enableCollisionsWithLayer()\fP for a linked pair of layers\&. Connected PhysicsBodies suppress their mutual contacts unless each connecting constraint allows them\&. Multiple shapes on the same body do not collide with one another\&. Contacts between linked layers using different solvers use basic impulse response\&.

.PP
A solid collider uses its owner's body by default\&. Without a body it acts as an externally positioned, immovable surface with no simulated velocity\&. Use a kinematic \fBPhysicsBody\fP for a moving platform that must carry or push objects\&. \fBsetPhysicsBody()\fP explicitly contributes a \fBPart\fP's geometry to a compound body; \fBuseOwnerPhysics()\fP restores the default association\&. Sensors report overlaps without impulses and work without any physical body\&.

.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
Both \fBSprite\fP and \fBPart\fP owners advance automatically\&. Native contact callbacks and opted-in eventType_ColliderContact events run after solving\&. Callbacks can remove colliders, bodies, owners or layers; contact payloads describe the solved frame, so another callback may already have detached a referenced collider\&.
.RE
.PP
.PP
.nf
const layer = pdg\&.createSpriteLayer();
layer\&.enableCollisions();
const sprite = layer\&.createSprite();
const foot = sprite\&.createPart('foot');
foot\&.setupPhysicsBody(1, 10);
foot\&.setupCollider()\&.setCircle(8)\&.setWantsContactEvents(true);
sprite\&.addHandler(new pdg\&.IEventHandler(function(event) {
    if (event\&.phase === pdg\&.collision_Begin && event\&.collider === foot\&.collider) {
        console\&.log('Foot contacted shape ' + event\&.otherShape);
    }
    return true;
}), pdg\&.eventType_ColliderContact);
.fi
.PP

.PP
Retained handles remain queryable after removal, using the final transform; callbacks and physical associations are cleared\&. Initial Sprite/Layer snapshots preserve collider geometry/configuration, compound body links and constraints\&. Use a Layer snapshot for links between Sprites\&. Callback filters and contact handlers cannot be saved; reinstall them after loading\&. Native callers can also use independent \fBCollider\fP and CollisionWorld objects for custom owner types\&.

.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBPhysicsBody\fP, \fBPhysicsConstraint\fP, \fBColliderContact\fP
.RE
.PP

.PP
\fBGeometry sources and explicit additions\fP
.RS 4

.RE
.PP
Operation  Frame/animation source  Caller-added shapes  \fBSprite\&.setupFrameCollider\fP / setupAnimationCollider  Selects the source and follows subsequent artwork updates  Clears previous geometry when selecting the source  addCircle / addCapsule / addBox / addPolygon / addImageMask  Continues updating  Adds a persistent shape in owner-local coordinates  removeShape  Throws for a source-controlled ID  Removes that addition only  setCircle / setCapsule / setBox / setPolygon / setImageMask  Stops following artwork  Replaces all geometry with the supplied shape  clearShapes  Stops following artwork  Removes all geometry  

.PP
Source updates preserve IDs by frame or authored box name\&. Source IDs may be inactive while an animation box is absent, and return when the box reappears\&. \fBgetShapeCount()\fP/getShapeId() enumerate the currently present shapes\&. \fBgetShapeName()\fP returns the authored box name, "frame" for a frame source, or an empty string for an explicit shape\&. Contacts aggregate convex pieces under each public shape ID\&.

.PP
 
.SH "Member Function Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "uint addBox (\fBRect\fP bounds)"

.PP
Add a local rectangle\&. Existing shape IDs remain unchanged\&. Shapes follow the owner’s position, rotation, scale and parent transforms\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIbounds\fP Finite local bounds with positive width and height\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
Stable nonzero shape ID, or collisionShape_None for NoCollider\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "uint addCapsule (\fBPoint\fP start, \fBPoint\fP end, number radius)"

.PP
Add a capsule while retaining existing shapes\&. Uses the geometry and transform rules in \fBcollider_capsule_geometry\fP\&. The new capsule has a stable ID\&. Existing shape IDs and any frame/animation geometry source remain intact; later source updates preserve this addition\&. Invalid input leaves the collider unchanged\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIstart\fP Finite local center of the first cap\&. 
.br
\fIend\fP Finite local center of the second cap; may equal start\&. 
.br
\fIradius\fP Finite positive radius in owner-local distance units\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The new nonzero shape ID, or collisionShape_None for NoCollider\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBsetCapsule()\fP, \fBremoveShape()\fP, \fBgetShapeType()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "uint addCircle (number radius, \fBPoint\fP center = \fR\fBPoint\fP(0,0)\fP)"

.PP
Add a local circle\&. Existing shape IDs remain unchanged\&. Shapes follow the owner’s position, rotation, scale and parent transforms\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIradius\fP Finite positive radius in owner-local units\&. 
.br
\fIcenter\fP Finite local center; defaults to the origin\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
Stable nonzero shape ID, or collisionShape_None for NoCollider\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "uint addImageMask (\fBImage\fP image, \fBRect\fP localBounds, int alphaThreshold = \fR128\fP)"

.PP
Copy opaque image pixels into collision geometry\&. Uses the entire supplied image, mapped to localBounds\&. Pixels with alpha at least alphaThreshold become merged convex rectangles; transparent holes and disconnected islands remain empty\&. Geometry is copied, so subsequent pixel edits require another call\&. An entirely transparent image has no contact area\&. Named images can reload discarded CPU pixels; unavailable pixels throw\&. At most 65536 convex pieces are supported\&. See \fBcollider_geometry_sources\fP\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIimage\fP \fBImage\fP to sample; use a frame image for a single strip frame\&. 
.br
\fIlocalBounds\fP Finite rectangle with positive dimensions in owner-local coordinates\&. 
.br
\fIalphaThreshold\fP Integer from 1 through 255; defaults to 128\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
One stable shape ID for the complete mask\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "uint addPolygon (array vertices)"

.PP
Add a simple local polygon, including concave outlines\&. Copies the outline and decomposes concave regions into convex solver pieces, retaining one public shape ID\&. Collinear edge points and a repeated closing point are accepted; crossings, touching edges, zero-area outlines and nonfinite points are rejected without changing existing geometry\&. Basic and Chipmunk use the same decomposition\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIvertices\fP Three through 4096 finite Points in perimeter order, clockwise or counterclockwise\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
Stable nonzero shape ID, or collisionShape_None for NoCollider\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "uint addPolygon (\fBPolygon\fP polygon)"

.PP
Copy collision geometry from a \fBPolygon\fP\&. The \fBPolygon\fP is copied; later edits to it do not change the collider\&. Concave outlines preserve their gaps through convex decomposition\&. See \fBcollider_geometry_sources\fP\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIpolygon\fP A simple polygon in owner-local coordinates\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The stable ID of the added shape\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBCollider\fP clearShapes ()"

.PP
Remove every collision shape\&. The collider remains attached and keeps its filters, material and body association\&.

.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
This object, for chaining\&. 
.RE
.PP

