.SS "\fBCollider\fP setCapsule (\fBPoint\fP start, \fBPoint\fP end, number radius)"

.PP
Replace all geometry with one capsule\&. The capsule consists of the line segment between start and end, expanded by radius in every direction\&. Endpoints are the centers of the rounded ends in owner-local coordinates\&. Total length is the distance between the endpoints plus twice the radius, and width is twice the radius\&. Coincident endpoints behave as a circle while retaining collisionShape_Capsule as the public type\&.

.PP
Coordinates are copied\&. Validation finishes before existing shapes are replaced; the capsule receives a fresh shape ID\&. This stops any frame/animation geometry source, while preserving collider settings, owner/body association, mass and inertia\&. NoCollider ignores the operation\&.

.PP
Queries and both solvers use exact capsule geometry under translation, rotation, reflection and uniform scale\&. Nonuniform scale or shear uses a convex outline with 16 straight segments per semicircle plus the two straight sides; coincident endpoints use the same 32-sided approximation as a deformed circle\&. All pieces remain one public shape ID\&. Capsule geometry and IDs survive scene snapshots; older readers without capsule support reject that shape kind\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIstart\fP Finite local center of the first cap\&. 
.br
\fIend\fP Finite local center of the second cap; may equal start\&. 
.br
\fIradius\fP Finite positive radius in owner-local distance units\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
This \fBCollider\fP, for chaining\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
Available in both GUI and headless builds; artwork is not required\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBExample\fP
.RS 4

.PP
.nf
const sprite = new pdg\&.Sprite();
sprite\&.setupPhysicsBody(2, 30);
sprite\&.setupCollider()\&.setCapsule(new pdg\&.Point(\-12, 0), new pdg\&.Point(12, 0), 3);
const shape = sprite\&.collider\&.getShapeId(0);
const start = sprite\&.collider\&.getCapsuleStart(shape);

.fi
.PP
.RE
.PP
The example creates a capsule 30 units long and 6 units wide\&. Add the \fBSprite\fP to an active collision-enabled layer to simulate contacts\&.

.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBaddCapsule()\fP, \fBgetCapsuleStart()\fP, \fBgetCapsuleEnd()\fP, \fBgetCapsuleRadius()\fP, \fBsetCircle()\fP 
.RE
.PP

